# pipeOS hardware watchdog (Intel iTCO, nowayout=0). Read by our own
# /etc/init.d/watchdog (#247), which also reads the card: WATCHDOG=kernel
# (default) arms, WATCHDOG=off leaves the device closed. Change it with
# `pipeos watchdog kernel|off`, not here.
#
# Plain interval petting only, on purpose: busybox watchdog has no
# test-command support, and a custom health-conditional petter would be a
# new always-on daemon whose own bugs hard-reset the box. A wedged kernel
# or dead userspace stops the petting and the TCO reboots us; with the
# boot selfcheck + mount-race retries, a reboot is a full recovery, and the
# boot report names the watchdog as the cause.
# 60 s hardware timeout (decided 2026-09-15; was 30), petted every 20 s.
WATCHDOG_DEV="/dev/watchdog0"
WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT=60
WATCHDOG_INTERVAL=20
